    summary:  "Organization Model Enhancement, Epic 4 of the CargoWise gap-analysis roadmap: Customer Hierarchy & Named-Account Unification. New nullable, self-referential customers.parent_customer_id (ON DELETE SET NULL, enforced live since foreign_keys=ON is set globally) — a plain ADD COLUMN, not the heavier table-rebuild v0.54.0's shipment_schedules.shipment_id needed, since this is a brand new nullable column rather than an existing NOT NULL one being loosened. New shared server-side resolveCustomerGroup(customerId) helper — given any customer id in a hierarchy, walks up to the root ancestor then back down to every descendant, so a rollup report gets the same consolidated group regardless of which member's id it started from. Deliberately read-side only: the three independent customer-pointer mechanisms flagged in the original gap analysis (shipment fixed FKs, shipment_parties, contracts.named_account_id) keep writing plain denormalized customer_id/customer_name pairs exactly as they already do everywhere else in this codebase — this doesn't unify or change that convention, it just reads across it for reporting, avoiding a much larger and riskier write-path refactor for a reporting-only need.\n\nNew Parent Customer picker on the customer Profile tab (CustomerCombobox, unrestricted — no roleFilter, since a parent relationship isn't a role) with server-side cycle detection (rejects both direct self-parenting and a deeper A-parent-B/B-parent-A loop, which would otherwise make resolveCustomerGroup's own walk infinite) and a friendly rejection message. Margin/GP reporting (GET /api/margin/summary, DashboardPage.jsx's Margin tab) gains a new By Customer breakdown (grouped by each shipment's Principal, falling back to Consignee — the same responsibleParty precedence invoiceGenerator.js already uses) with a 'Roll up by parent' toggle: off by default, on remaps every line to its hierarchy's root customer via resolveCustomerGroup before aggregating, so a multinational shipper's shipments booked under several regional customer records show as one consolidated row. Carrier Booking's existing 'Client' field (the linked contract's own Named Account) gains a small 'Part of {parent}' caption when that customer has a parent set — a single-shipment display gets useful context, not a numeric rollup, since there's nothing to aggregate on one shipment's own client field.\n\nNew tests/customer-hierarchy.test.js (17 assertions: parent/child round-trip, bogus-parent rejection, self-parent rejection, cycle rejection, the flat-vs-rolled-up margin math including the ON DELETE SET NULL cascade when a parent is deleted) — full suite green (18 files), clean build. Verified live via CDP: the Parent Customer field resolves and displays correctly on a real branch/subsidiary pair, and toggling 'Roll up by parent' on the Margin tab correctly collapses two separate customer rows into one combined row under the parent's name.",
