    summary:  "Organization Model Enhancement, Epic 2 of the CargoWise gap-analysis roadmap: Credit Control. New credit_limit/credit_terms_days/credit_hold/credit_hold_reason fields on customers (surfaced in the Profile tab's Billing section, right alongside Currency) tie directly into the already-shipped invoicing infrastructure (generateInvoices, ShipmentAccountingInvoicesPage.jsx) rather than needing a new page. A credit_hold on the Shipper, Consignee, Principal, or the linked contract's Named Account now hard-blocks the Generate Invoice / Generate Per-Container Invoices actions with a modal naming exactly which party and why — existing cost lines and documents on the shipment stay fully visible and editable, only the act of generating a NEW invoice is blocked. New GET /api/customers/:id/credit-status resolves outstanding AR by summing every CONFIRMED (non-voided) FR01/FR02 invoice for shipments where the customer is Principal or Consignee, resolving each invoice's real dollar total via source_cost_line_ids (the same field the v0.53.0 invoice-reversal feature introduced for exactly this 'what was this invoice actually for' question) with the identical live-container-scoped fallback for older invoices. When outstanding AR plus the invoice about to be generated would exceed the limit, a separate soft-warning modal shows the projected total with Cancel/Generate Anyway — generation is never hard-blocked on amount alone, only on an explicit hold, matching the epic's own scoped decision that a real hard block needs a proper AR-aging view this app doesn't have yet.\n\nOne real design gap caught and fixed during CDP verification, not just in the plan: the first implementation of the over-limit check only looked at prior confirmed invoices, so it would never catch the very first invoice that actually pushes a customer over their limit — only ones generated after they were already over. Fixed by having resolveCreditGate (src/utils/invoiceGenerator.js) accept the prospective new invoice's own dollar amount (scoped by whether it's a consolidated or per-container generation, mirroring the existing currency-check's own scoping) and compare outstandingAr + newAmountUsd against the limit, not outstandingAr alone. New tests/customer-credit-control.test.js (28 assertions: credit field round-trip, outstanding-AR computation across two invoices, reversal correctly excluding a voided invoice from the total, hold set/clear including reason cleanup) — full suite green (16 files), clean build. Verified live via CDP end-to-end: a held customer's invoice generation shows the exact blocking modal with their name and hold reason and produces zero documents; clearing the hold and lowering the limit below an uninvoiced line's amount correctly shows the projected-total warning modal instead, with Generate Anyway still available.",
