    date:     "2026-08-01",
    codename: "Catalog",
    summary:  "A fourth live bug on the same feature: transit time showed '0d' for a real 2-leg TSP catalog match with an 8-day door-to-door span. Root cause: POST /api/schedules (the Schedule Generator's create route) hardcoded transit_days to the literal value 0 at insert time — it was never derived from the schedule's own etd/eta, unlike every other sailing source (mockSailings()/maerskSchedules() both compute it correctly from real date math). Fixed by computing it as the whole-journey ETD->ETA span in days, which naturally folds in any transshipment hub dwell time between legs instead of undercounting it — a TSP with a multi-day layover at the hub is not the sum of each leg's own transit, it's the full door-to-door span. Added a one-time startup backfill for schedules already created with this bug (source='generated', transit_days still 0, real etd/eta present) — safe to re-run, only touches rows the bug actually affected. Verified live: the exact reported schedule (AVATR ex KIRAN ASYA, NLRTM->USNYC via USMIA) now correctly shows 8d after the backfill, and a freshly created TSP schedule with a 4-day hub dwell correctly totals 14d end-to-end via the API. Also investigated a separate report of inconsistent Route Legs table formatting between the Contracts & Schedules page and the shipment Edit form — direct side-by-side comparison via automated browser testing found no actual discrepancy; both already render the shared LegsTable component identically with no overlaps on a fresh shipment.",
