    summary:  "Two real bugs found live on the v0.54.0 catalog-search feature, both user-reported directly against a real shipment (SHP-W942AJ). First: 'Add Sailing' results looked artificially constrained/wrong — traced to the new catalogSailings() query having no is_mock exclusion, so it was resurrecting old shipment_schedules rows saved back when Add Sailing always inserted a row for any picked sailing, including synthetic 'DEMO ...' ones — confirmed live, 4 stale rows named 'DEMO DULCIMER'/'DEMO CADENZA' were surfacing tagged source:catalog as if they were real curated data. Fixed with an is_mock=0 filter on the catalog query. Second: the Configure Legs modal's Vessel field was a plain text input with no connection to the real vessel registry, and there was no way to set a per-leg carrier at all (only one carrier for the whole schedule, at the top level) — real TSP sailings routinely change carrier at a transshipment hub. Vessel column now reuses the existing VesselCombobox (real /api/vessels/search typeahead, same component ShipmentFormPage's own vessel picker uses) with a compact selected-vessel chip; a new Carrier column (CarrierCombobox per row) was added, backed by a new schedule_legs.carrier column — the schedule's own top-level carrier now derives from leg 1's carrier when set, same fallback pattern already used for vessel/voyage/service. tests/schedule-catalog.test.js gained 7 new assertions (stale-mock-exclusion regression, per-leg carrier/vesselImo round-trip) — 57 total, full suite green (13 files, 546 assertions), clean build. Verified live via CDP/Cypress: confirmed the stale rows no longer appear and a real search correctly falls through to fresh demo data instead, and confirmed the vessel field's autocomplete genuinely hits the vessels API and the carrier column renders and works per leg.",
